    {
      "title": "Hong Kong pro-democracy activist Joshua Wong sentenced to 10 years in prison in national security case",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/05/hong-kong-joshua-wong-sentenced-national-security-case",
      "description": "<p>Wong, 30, has been imprisoned since 2020 and is the only activist in Hong Kong prosecuted twice under national security law</p><p>Hong Kong activist <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joshua-wong\">Joshua Wong</a> was sentenced on Thursday to 10 years in prison after pleading guilty to “foreign collusion”, his second conviction under a national security law that critics say has been used to silence political opposition in the city.</p><p>Wong, who <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/may/14/joshua-wong-the-student-who-risked-the-wrath-of-beijing-its-about-turning-the-impossible-into-the-possible\">rose to prominence</a> as the teenage face of Hong Kong’s 2014 pro-democracy demonstrations, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/02/hong-kong-pro-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-collusion-china\">submitted his plea</a> in September. He had been accused of working with the exiled Hong Kong activist <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nathan-law\">Nathan Law</a> to urge foreign powers to impose sanctions, blockades or other hostile measures against China.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/05/hong-kong-joshua-wong-sentenced-national-security-case\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-05T03:28:52"
    },
    {
      "title": "Joshua Wong, Hong Kong Democracy Activist, Is Sentenced to 10 Years in Prison",
